WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.141
- I bought a friend off the internet.

00:00:02.141 --> 00:00:04.474
(fun music)

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:09.430
People are selling
imaginary friends on eBay,

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:11.730
and I'm gonna buy one.

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:15.330
I didn't know that imaginary
friends were transferable.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.560
I thought you had to imagine it yourself,

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.700
put in the work, you get your friend.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.240
They are extremely expensive.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.010
There's one that's $600.

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:27.250
There are two that are $1,000.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.260
Obviously, it seems weird
to pay money for a friend.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.960
That's not how friendship
is supposed to work.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:36.920
I just paid $20 to get
a friend in the mail.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:41.140
So, bad news, my $20 friend

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.580
never came.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:45.220
I'm worried that my friend
is just lost in the mail,

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:47.450
and that seems horrible.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:50.450
But in the meantime, I
really want a friend,

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:54.510
so I went back on eBay, and
I found a different friend.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:56.550
This one is $50.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:00.230
Hopefully this friend comes
in the mail this time.

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:01.829
My friend is here, my friend is here.

00:01:01.829 --> 00:01:03.250
(upbeat music)

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:05.240
This is the box that I
received in the mail.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.400
Welcome, friend.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:09.460
There's something in here,
so that's a little scary.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:10.293
You know what?

00:01:10.293 --> 00:01:12.950
Let's just open this box,
and meet my brand new friend.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:15.286
Whatever it is, it's
wrapped in a paper towel.

00:01:15.286 --> 00:01:17.610
I'm so scared, how is this a friend?

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:18.572
Oh, my God.

00:01:18.572 --> 00:01:21.072
(eerie music)

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:27.210
My $50 imaginary friend box included

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:30.180
this Granny Smith apple and an envelope.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.670
Maybe this was food for
the imaginary friend,

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:35.110
in case they got hungry on the journey.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:37.670
Let's open this envelope
and get more information.

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:39.360
My new friend is Andy.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:42.260
Andy, I assume that you're
in here, so welcome.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:44.390
Have a seat, make yourself comfortable.

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:46.650
Do you mind being in this Buzzfeed video?

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.960
It's a lot all at once, I get that.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.570
"Thank you for your purchase.

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:51.880
"He is an amazing friend.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.990
"And he was always next
to me when I needed him.

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:56.270
"I've talked to him, and he
is very excited to meet you,

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:58.740
"and see his new home."

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:01.160
You know, I didn't think about that.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:03.460
Are you supposed to live with me?

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:06.410
Normally, your friends don't
necessarily live with you.

00:02:07.428 --> 00:02:10.270
You don't have a place to stay?

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:11.440
Okay, well, we'll talk about it.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.940
You can definitely sleep on
my couch at least one night.

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:15.570
We'll talk about it.

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:19.140
Cool, this also says that
apples are Andy's favorite food.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:20.100
So, that's interesting.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.040
So, you're from California.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:24.080
Andy was just saying that it's weird

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.710
to travel through the mail,
which I totally understand.

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:27.790
I'm so sorry.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:30.019
Okay, so, Andy, now that you're here,

00:02:30.019 --> 00:02:31.240
what do you wanna do now?

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:33.600
We can do whatever you want.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:34.860
You don't know?

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:39.520
Okay, what do friends normally do?

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:41.270
I'm gonna show Andy around.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:43.010
And try to show him a good time.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:46.300
Andy, if you love apples, I
have to show you something.

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:48.840
Andy, check this out.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.530
Look at all these apples.

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:52.880
He's excited, he's gonna
take like five apples.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:56.350
- Yeah, who is it?

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:58.008
- [Joanna] This is Andy.

00:02:58.008 --> 00:03:00.350
- Okay, cool.

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:03.130
Oh, Andy, hey, good to meet you.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.450
Where did you guys meet, on eBay?

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:08.280
You did not.

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:12.977
- Sure.
- What?

00:03:12.977 --> 00:03:15.560
(gentle music)

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:17.860
- Hey, Andy.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.510
I feel like immediately creeped out,

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:21.900
like there is a friend there.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:23.550
- This is some dark-sided shit.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:26.530
I don't want no part of this dark-sided--

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:27.920
Get away from me, devil.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:30.503
(gentle music)

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:42.180
- Hi, Andy.

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:45.381
- What do you like to do, Andy?

00:03:45.381 --> 00:03:47.880
(gentle music)

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:49.040
- Andy's pretty funny.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.270
He does not like you though.

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:56.540
- Okay, so, Andy, what do
you think of New York so far?

00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:59.420
You miss California?

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:02.260
That's fair, I would too, it's very cold.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:04.800
Is there anything you've always
wanted to do in New York?

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.520
Get more apples?

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.830
Okay, we'll get you as
many apples as you want.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.971
No, we'll get you more apples, it's fine.

00:04:12.971 --> 00:04:15.554
(gentle music)

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:18.410
- Jo, who are you talking to?

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:23.006
Is he sitting in this seat right here?

00:04:23.006 --> 00:04:24.589
Aw, hey, Andy?

00:04:24.589 --> 00:04:25.422
- [Joanna] Yeah.

00:04:25.422 --> 00:04:26.350
- Hey, Andy, how you doing?

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:28.059
- Well, what do you wanna do now?

00:04:28.059 --> 00:04:30.220
(gentle music)

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:33.900
Okay, we don't have to
do everything together.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:36.240
You know, like you're free to leave.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:38.700
You can go exploring on
your own if you want.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:39.720
Like, please don't feel like

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.100
you have to be tethered to me.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:42.550
Oh, okay, okay, you're going?

00:04:45.638 --> 00:04:47.530
Okay, see you later.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.510
I'm slightly concerned
'cause I can't find Andy.

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:56.500
He hasn't been here for awhile,

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:58.600
and I don't know where he went.

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:01.420
And I'm afraid maybe he's
mad at me, I don't know.

00:05:04.317 --> 00:05:05.150
- Who's Andy?

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:08.180
- That's so true.

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:11.320
- We're just hanging out with Andy.

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:13.980
- Oh, my God, wait, Andy, tell your story.

00:05:16.101 --> 00:05:17.740
(both chuckle)

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:19.678
- Oh, my God, you are so funny.

00:05:19.678 --> 00:05:21.130
- [Woman In Purple
Shirt] Oh, my God, Andy.

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:22.730
- We're gonna go apple
picking this weekend,

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:26.800
like upstate.
- Yeah.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.675
- I mean, you can come.
- Yeah.

00:05:28.675 --> 00:05:30.810
- Just doesn't seem like
something you'd be into.

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:34.290
- Okay, let's just get on
the subway and head home.

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:38.190
You can go to bed early if
you want, I'm pretty tired.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.854
Can I get you anything, like
a glass of water or something?

00:05:46.854 --> 00:05:49.040
(gentle music)

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:52.890
Oh, crap, I don't have any apples.

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:54.420
I'm so sorry.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.840
Would a tomato work maybe?

00:05:58.380 --> 00:05:59.330
No, okay.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.330
Okay, Andy, I got you
a pillow and blanket,

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:03.060
so you can go to sleep.

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:04.630
Let me know if you're not warm enough.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:07.360
I just want you to know that
I'm glad that you're here,

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:09.550
and I'm glad you're my friend.

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:12.090
And hopefully, tomorrow
we can have a better day.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:14.400
Sweet dreams.
(gentle music)

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:15.390
What was that?

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:18.366
Okay, good night.

00:06:18.366 --> 00:06:21.240
(eerie music)

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:24.990
I feel a little weird going to bed knowing

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:28.210
that Andy is sleeping in my living room.

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:30.861
But I'm sure it's fine.

00:06:30.861 --> 00:06:32.040
(sighs) Good night.

00:06:33.147 --> 00:06:35.090
(bottles clanking)
What was that?

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:56.600
I'm gonna go see if Andy's awake.

00:06:57.846 --> 00:07:00.346
(eerie music)

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:16.430
I think he left.

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:20.890
I don't know where Andy went.

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:23.420
I hope he's okay, I miss him.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:27.090
I'm grateful for the time we
had together, however short.

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:29.780
The truth is, real friendship can't

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:32.040
be purchased off the internet.

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:37.040
- This sounds more like an
imaginary escort, I would say.

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:38.950
- [Joanna] Wait, seriously?

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:41.690
- [Woman] Yeah, yeah,
you're paying for his time,

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:44.118
so he's an escort.

00:07:44.118 --> 00:07:45.318
- [Joanna] You're right.

